<DocsLayout title="With ForgeInject" section="examples">
  <h1>With ForgeInject</h1>
  <p class="text-lg text-muted-foreground mt-1 mb-8">Register ForgePush components as singletons in ForgeInject so they can be injected anywhere in the app — not just in AppDelegate.</p>

  <h2>Registration</h2>
  <p>Create a <code>ForgeRegisterProtocol</code> struct for push dependencies. Register each component as a singleton and add handlers inside the factory closure so the router is ready immediately on first resolve.</p>
  <CodeBlock code={registrationCode} title="PushDependencies.swift" />

  <h2>AppDelegate</h2>
  <p>Use <code>@ForgeInject</code> to resolve the push components. Set up the container in <code>application(_:didFinishLaunchingWithOptions:)</code> before the property wrappers are first accessed.</p>
  <CodeBlock code={appDelegateCode} title="AppDelegate.swift" />

  <h2>Consuming the Token Elsewhere</h2>
  <p>Because <code>PushTokenManager</code> is a singleton in the container, any view model can inject and observe it directly — no need to pass it through initializers. Remember that <code>tokenStream</code> emits <code>String?</code>.</p>
  <CodeBlock code={viewModelCode} title="TaskFlowSettingsViewModel.swift" />

